; ============================================================================
; GOLDEN_12_SYMBOLS.ERB - @label symbol table: duplicate resolution, event buckets
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Purpose : L2 proof for specs/loader.md Appendix D (symbol table / override rules).
; Evidence: - per-file SortLabel overwrites: ErbLoader.cs:514-518
;           - noneventLabelDic[name] = label (LAST definition wins): LabelDictionary.cs:60-68
;           - event labels: all registered, run in bucket order
;             ONLY(0) -> PRI(1) -> NORMAL(2) -> LATER(3): CalledFunction.cs:228-243
; Rules   : ASCII only, deterministic, no RAND, no state outside RESULT.
; Expected: SECTION:DUP-METHOD  -> DUP-METHOD=2
;           SECTION:DUP-PLAIN   -> DUP-PLAIN=3  (via RESULT:2; plain RETURN zeroes RESULT:0)
;           SECTION:EVENT-BUCKET-> prints a reminder only; the marker order
;                                  (PRI, NORMAL, LATER) is observed at turn end.
; Notes   : - Same-file duplicates do NOT abort loading. Load time emits one
;             level-1 warning per shadowed NON-EVENT definition:
;             G12_FUNC x1 + G12_PLAIN x2 = 3 lines, before any run output (see runbook 8).
;             Event duplicates (EVENTTURNEND) produce NO warning
;             (ErbLoader.cs:443 only warns when !IsEvent).
;           - PRINTV G12_PLAIN() is deliberately NOT used: a plain @label is not a
;             method, so expression-position use throws UsedNonMethodFunc
;             (IdentifierDictionary.cs:566-569). CALL G12_PLAIN + RESULT is faithful.
;           - 3 x EVENTTURNEND in one file: definition order is NORMAL, PRI,
;             LATER while execution order is PRI, NORMAL, LATER - that reorder
;             is the observable proof of bucket ordering.
; ============================================================================
@GOLDEN_SYMBOLS
	PRINTL === SECTION:DUP-METHOD ===
	PRINTFORML DUP-METHOD={G12_FUNC()}
	PRINTL === SECTION:DUP-PLAIN ===
	RESULT:2 = 0
	CALL G12_PLAIN
	PRINTFORML DUP-PLAIN={RESULT:2}
	PRINTL === SECTION:EVENT-BUCKET ===
	PRINTFORML EVENT-DEFS=3 EXPECT-ORDER=PRI,NORMAL,LATER
	PRINTFORML EVENT-BUCKET-REMARK=collect one turn end to see markers
	RETURN

; --- 1) same-file duplicate #FUNCTION: the later definition must win ---
@G12_FUNC
#FUNCTION
	RETURNF 1

@G12_FUNC
#FUNCTION
	RETURNF 2

; --- 2) same-file duplicate plain @label: the later definition must win ---
@G12_PLAIN
	RESULT:2 = 1
	RETURN

@G12_PLAIN
	RESULT:2 = 2
	RETURN

@G12_PLAIN
	RESULT:2 = 3
	RETURN

; --- 3) event bucket order: PRI(1) -> NORMAL(2) -> LATER(3) ---
@EVENTTURNEND
	RESULT:1 = RESULT:1 | 2
	PRINTFORML EVENT-BUCKET-NORMAL

@EVENTTURNEND
#PRI
	RESULT:1 = RESULT:1 | 1
	PRINTFORML EVENT-BUCKET-PRI

@EVENTTURNEND
#LATER
	RESULT:1 = RESULT:1 | 4
	PRINTFORML EVENT-BUCKET-LATER
